text:
alex: Heads up — I'm going to move the payments-uploader ServiceAccount into payments-ns so the imagePullSecret and secret ownership live in the same namespace. Planning to change the terraform k8s_service_account resource. Quick sanity check: will this require any extra RBAC or secret CRD changes? I don't expect downtime but want a quick review.

 taylor: @alex sounds reasonable. Can you paste the tf diff here? Also, will the SA need the IRSA annotation (eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn) or is that handled by the existing role binding?

 alex: Pasting the minimal diff I'm planning to apply:

 ```hcl
 resource "kubernetes_service_account" "payments_uploader" {
   metadata {
     name      = "payments-uploader"
     namespace = "payments-ns"
     annotations = {
       "eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn" = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/payments-uploader-role"
     }
   }

   automount_service_account_token = false
 }
 ```

 taylor: Okay. A couple things: if the uploader pod uses a sidecar that calls AWS STS via projected tokens, you need `automount_service_account_token = true`. If it's only an initContainer that grabs creds and exits, false is fine. Also confirm the role ARN is the right one for the new namespace.

 maria: Which workloads are we talking about? Payments uploader deployment or the telemetry sidecar? If the sidecar needs a projected token, setting automount to true is necessary OR you need to add a projected `ServiceAccountToken` volume in the pod spec. We usually prefer automount=true for these services to avoid pod spec churn.

 alex: Good catch. It is the uploader + a small metrics sidecar that talks to S3. I'll flip automount to true and add the IRSA annotation. Updating diff now.

 ```hcl
 resource "kubernetes_service_account" "payments_uploader" {
   metadata {
     name      = "payments-uploader"
     namespace = "payments-ns"
     annotations = {
       "eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn" = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/payments-uploader-role"
     }
   }

   automount_service_account_token = true
 }
 ```

 infra-bot: terraform validate: passed. tflint: no issues. plan requested by @alex.

 maria: I ran a quick `terraform plan` against staging and it shows a small change (annotation + automount flip). Plan excerpt: 

 ```
 # kubernetes_service_account.payments_uploader will be updated in-place
 ~ resource "kubernetes_service_account" "payments_uploader" {
     automount_service_account_token = false -> true
     metadata {
       annotations = {
         + "eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn" = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/payments-uploader-role"
       }
     }
 }
 Plan: 0 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy.
 ```

 taylor: Nice and small. Let's run this in staging first and do a canary rollout in prod (scale down/up or gradual deployment). Also add a note in the release doc that imagePullSecrets remain unchanged and we're not moving secret data.

 alex: Will do the staging apply tonight at 22:00 PT. I'll also trigger a rolling restart of deployments in payments-ns after the apply. Tagging @oncall in case anything weird pops.

 taylor: Ack. Please paste the apply output when done.

 maria: Staging apply finished — no secret diffs, SA updated, sidecar token requests look normal. Did a rolling restart; no auth errors in logs. :thumbsup:

 alex: Thanks all. I'll schedule prod canary on Tuesday during the 02:00 UTC low-traffic window. Will follow up here after prod apply.

 taylor: +1 from me.

 infra-bot: deploy-bot: staging-apply completed by maria at 2025-11-03T05:12:34Z.

 maria: Leaving a short postmortem note in the runbook in case we need to revert.

 alex: perfect — closing the loop, thanks everyone. :party_parrot:
